  "body": "Found while fixing #1329 (PR #1346).\n\nWhat happens: `AlignPartToSetup::align_from_axes` with both +Y and +X picked builds the new alignment through the held one. Applied a second time to the same picks, the turn should be the identity, but the composed alignment comes out a float hair away from what the setup holds (e.g. origin y `-7.499999999999999` against `-7.5`). `change_of` (`crates/app/src/commands/setup_align.rs`) compares `next == prev` exactly, so it accepts the change. The result is a no-op undo step where the user should get \"setup '...' already holds the part that way\". The in-plane path avoids this because `in_plane_turn_deg` snaps to exact quarter turns. This happens in both the GUI (Setups page \"Part axes\" Apply) and MCP `set_part_axes`.\n\nExpected: re-applying picks that already land refuses with \"already holds the part that way\", or `align_from_axes` returns the held alignment unchanged when the turn is the identity within tolerance.\n\nDone means: re-applying the same two-axis picks refuses by name (pinned in `crates/app/tests/align_axes.rs` and/or `mcp_align_axes.rs`), and no tolerance change lets a real alignment change through as \"already held\".\n",
